
FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://dale.staging.shadowfax.in/api

# Shadowfax Reverse Pickup API

Using the Shadowfax Reverse Pickup API collection, developers can integrate our customer pickup platform into their applications. The API is designed to allow application developers to check Pincode serviceability, place and manage orders and then track order status till completion.

*Use this API if the use case is to return the picked item to your warehouse. If you want us to return the picked item
to the individual seller, please refer to [Reverse Pickup - Seller Delivery document](https://sfxreversepickupsellerdelivery.docs.apiary.io/).*


## Glossary

###DCs and Hubs
*DC*: Large facilities typically located in the outskirts of a city where all shipments(intercity and intracity both) are processed.<br>


*Hub*: Small facilities located across the city from where last-mile delivery and first mile pick up happens. 


####Following terms are defined with respect to a shipment's location
* Origin Hub:<br>
This is the first shadowfax facility where a packet reaches directly from seller or customer
* Origin DC:<br>
This is the first DC where a packet is sent from the client Warehouse or origin hub to process further.
* Destination Hub:<br>
This is the last shadowfax facility where a packet reaches before delivering to customer or seller
* Destination DC:<br>
This is last DC where a packet is sent before sending to destination hub or client Warehouse
* Via DC:<br>
All DCs other than origin and destination where a shipment has to go through. Manifest bags are not opened at these DCs and will be directly passed on to the next location.

####Type of Operations
* Forward Operations:<br>
Orders that are originating at client warehouse or seller side and are to be delivered to end customer.<br>
<br>
* Reverse Operations: <br>
Return orders that are originating at customer side or forward orders that could not be delivered to the customer and are to be returned to client warehouse or seller. <br>

####Miscellaneous
<br>
* AWBs: <br>
Unique Identification Number for each item/packet <br>
* LOR: <br>
Letter of Receipt, a document for acknowledging the delivery or receipt of shipments/ packets <br>
* POD(Proof of Delivery): <br>
A receipt of pickup and delivery of items



##Authentication
Shadowfax API uses Token Authentication. You will be shared Staging and Production API keys from the Shadowfax Team via an automated email.
<br><br>The `Authorization` header that should be used while sending request will look like:
<br>
`Token e43145811ca6e75cde2d232df3d41485` where `e43145811ca6e75cde2d232df3d41485` is the token shared.
<br>The `Authorization` value itself contains the Word “Token”.

##Requests
This is base URL.Please refer to endpoints to make actual request.The base URL for all requests to the Production Shadowfax Server is given below:<br>
|||
|------------|-----------|
|Staging|`https://dale.staging.shadowfax.in/api`|
|Production|`https://dale.shadowfax.in/api`|
   
All our API is REST-based. This means:  
* It makes use of standard HTTP verbs like GET, POST, DELETE.
* The API uses standard HTTP error responses to describe errors.
* Authentication is specified with HTTP Token Authentication.  

POST data should be encoded as standard `application/json`  
|Accepted Format||
|--------------------|--------------------|
|Date|(YYYY:MM:DD)|
|DateTime |(YYYY:MM:DD HH:MM:SS)|

##Responses
Shadowfax API uses HTTP status codes to indicate the status of your requests. This includes successful and unsuccessful responses.

* All responses are in [JSON]('http://www.json.org'). 

* All response Timestamps follow [ISO-8061]('https://www.w3.org/TR/NOTE-datetime') format.
    > Times are expressed in local time, together with a time zone offset in hours and minutes. A time zone offset of "+hh:mm" indicates that the date/time uses a local time zone which is "hh" hours and "mm" minutes ahead of UTC. A time zone offset of "-hh:mm" indicates that the date/time uses a local time zone which is "hh" hours and "mm" minutes behind UTC.
    
#### Status Codes

* 200 - OK: Everything went as planned.
* 400 - Bad Request: You did something wrong. Often a missing argument or parameter.
* 401 - Unauthorized: Authentication was incorrect.
* 404 - Not Found
* 500 - Internal Server Error: We had a problem processing the request.
* 503 - Service Unavailable: Try again later.

##Order States
A given pickup order can be in one of the following states. This state will be shared in the `status` field in the Order Tracking APIs.

|Order State                    |comment                                                  |Description                 |
|-------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|
| `New`                         | Item New at `<SFX Facility> `                             | When the pickup request is received in the Shadowfax system                         |
| `Assigned`                    | Item Assigned For Customer Pickup at `<SFX Facility>`     | When the pickup request is assigned to a pickup executive for pickup                |
| `Out For Pickup`              | Item Out For Pickup at `<SFX Facility>`                   | When the assigned pickup executive is Out for Pickup                                |
| `Picked`                      | Picked Successfully                                       | When the item is picked by the pickup executive                                     |
| `Received`                    | Received at hub Successfully                              | When the picked item is received at the hub                                         |
| `Received at Return DC`       | Received at Return DC Successfully                        | When the picked item is received at the Return DC |
| `Cancelled`                   | Refer [Appendix](#Appendix_cancelled) for detailed reasons of order Cancelled.| When the pickup request is cancelled                                                |
| `Cid`                         | Refer [Appendix](#Appendix_cid) for detailed reasons of Cid | When the pickup is delayed by the customer to another date                          |
| `Not Contactable`             | Refer [Appendix](#Appendix_nc) for detailed reasons of Not Contactable | When the customer is not contactable by the delivery executive                      |
| `Not Attempted`               | Refer [Appendix](#Appendix_na) for detailed reasons of Not Attempted                                      | When the assigned pickup executive couldn't attempt the pickup                      |
| `Returned To Client`          | Item Return To Origin Delivered at `<SFX Facility>`       | When the item is returned to the seller destination pincode hub              |
| `Undelivered`                 | Item Return to Origin Not Delivered at `<SFX Facility>`   | When there is a failed delivery to client warehouse or seller address               |
| `Lost`                        | Item Lost at `<SFX Facility>`                              | When the picked item is Lost in transit or at hub                                   |
| `QC Failed`                   | Refer [Appendix](#Appendix_qc) for detailed reasons of QC Failed | When doorstep QC is failed for the pickup item                                      |
| `On Hold`                     | Refer [Appendix](#Appendix_On_Hold) for detailed reasons of On Hold   | When the item is put On Hold on client orders or due to Operational Concerns  |
| `Item added to Bag`           | Item added to bag at `<SFX facility>`  | When the order is added to the bag    |            
| `Bag In Transit`              | Bag in transit from `<SFX Facility>` | This status signifies that the bag (Master Manifest) is in transit.    |            
| `Bag Received`                | Bag received at `<SFX Facility>` | This status signifies that the bag (Master Manifest) has been received at the destination facility |            
| `Received`                    | Item Return To Origin at `<SFX Facility>` | The Item Returned To Origin   |            
| `Item Misrouted`              | Item misrouted at `<SFX Facility>` |  The shipment reached to a wrong sfx facility  |            
| `Pincode Updated`             | Item destination pincode updated at `<SFX Facility>` | The Item destination pincode updated   |            
| `In Transit for Return`       | The Bag in transit return from `<SFX Facility>` | This status signifies that the bag (Master Manifest) is in transit during rts journey.|            
| `Bag in transit for return`   | Bag in transit for return at `<SFX Facility>`| The  Bag in transit for return at sfx facility  |            


##Push Callback API
We have built a generic PUSH API callback for the Reverse model. The client can enable it to get real-time notification of each push notification status change. 
### Callback Header details

The Standard callback header has below keys:

+ Headers

      Authorization: Token c6b780ae9250f3
      Content-Type: application/json

Here we have the capability to add/modify the hearder keys as shown in the example below:

+ Headers

    Content-Type: application/json
    Authorization: d5eecf30ae6eb8d158dc54c77178ab9
    account_name:  SF_ACC_STAGING


### Request Body details

The callback contains the below parameters:

* `awb_number` - Generated by Shadowfax while placing an order.
* `order_id` - client_order_id shared while placing an order.
* `event_timestamp` - event_timestamp of the current status.
* `current_location` - The current location of the order during the event.
* `comments` - Contains the remarks associated with the status.
* `event` - Current status id of the shipment
* `status` - Current status of the shipment
* `otp_verifed` - The value indicates whether the status was marked after OTP verification. The possible values are `"Y"/"N"/"NA"`. By Default `"NA"`.
* `rider_name` - The name of the rider delivering the order.The rider details are shared when the current status is Out For Pickup (ofp).
* `rider_contact` - The contact details of the rider delivering the order.The rider details are shared when the current status is Out For Pickup (ofp).
* `type` - The order type is shared over this field. eg: FWD/REV 
* `recepient_info` - This field contains proof of delivery, and it will be sent only when the current status has been delivered or RTS_D has been confirmed.
* `qc_images` - This field contains the images taken during QC failed.

This is the structure of the payload data(JSON) that will be pushed to your end.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "awb_number": "R18481863TMA",
            "order_id": "testwebhookrev10",
            "event_timestamp": "2022-06-17 16:54:49",
            "current_location": "DEL_Trinagar",
            "comments": "Item Assigned For Customer Pickup at DEL_Trinagar",
            "event": "assigned_for_pickup",
            "status": "Assigned",
            "otp_verifed" : "NA",
            "rider_name": null,
            "rider_contact": null,
            "client_id": 1707,
            "recipient_info":[],
            "qc_images": [],
            "type": "REV"
        }

When we want to send a push message to your server, we need to make an API call to a push service. API call would require the following callback details, which can be configured via the Client Portal on the Webhook tab.

`The appropriate URL implemented at your end to trigger a push message(Mandatory).`

`Authentication Key(Non mandatory).`

|Order State                    |comment                                                  |Description                 |
|-------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|
| `Assigned`                    | Item Assigned For Customer Pickup at `<SFX Facility>`                             | When the pickup request is received in the Shadowfax system                         |
| `Out For Pickup`              | Item Out For Pickup at `<SFX Facility>`                   | When the assigned pickup executive is Out for Pickup                                |
| `Picked`                      | Picked Successfully                                       | When the item is picked by the pickup executive                                     |
| `Received at Hub`             |Received at hub Successfully                              | When the picked item is received at the hub                                         |
| `Received at Return DC`       | Item Received at RTS DC at `<SFX Facility>`                       | When the picked item is received at the Return DC |
| `Cancelled`                   | Refer [Appendix](#Appendix_cancelledpushapiwarehouse) for detailed reasons of order Cancelled.| When the pickup request is cancelled                                                |
| `Cid`                         | Refer [Appendix](#Appendix_cidpushapiwarehouse) for detailed reasons of Cid | When the pickup is delayed by the customer to another date                          |
| `Not Contactable`             | Refer [Appendix](#Appendix_ncpushapiwarehouse) for detailed reasons of Not Contactable | When the customer is not contactable by the delivery executive                      |
| `Not Attempted`               | Refer [Appendix](#Appendix_napushapiwarehouse) for detailed reasons of Not able to attempt                                       | When the assigned pickup executive couldn't attempt the pickup                      |
| `Returned To Client`          | Item Return To Seller Delivered at `<SFX Facility>`       | When the item is returned to the seller destination pincode hub              |
| `Undelivered`                 | Item Return to Seller Not Delivered at `<SFX Facility>`   | When there is a failed delivery to client warehouse or seller address               |
| `Lost`                        | Item Lost at `<SFX Facility>`                              | When the picked item is Lost in transit or at hub                                   |
| `QC Failed`                   | <Order status Remark> | When doorstep QC is failed for the pickup item                                      |
| `On Hold`                     | Refer [Appendix](#Appendix_On_Holdpushapiwarehouse) for detailed reasons of On Hold   | When the item is put On Hold on client orders or due to Operational Concerns. |
| `Returned To Client`          | Item Return To Origin Delivered at `<SFX Facility>`                           |  The Item Return To Origin Delivered     |
| `Undelivered`                 | Item Return to Origin Not Delivered at `<SFX Facility>`                          |   The Item Return to Origin Not Delivered        |
| `ReOpen`                      | Product is reopened                              |       The product reopend for delivery     |


##QC Process
We follow the app-based doorstep QC process for all the eligible shipments picked up by our delivery executives.
Rules for the QC process are currently based on the *Return Reason* shared by the client. These rules can be configured in our internal Operations portal, for which details can be taken from the Sales POC.

In Order Tracking APIs, please look for the values of the following fields in the SKU details - 

* `picked` - If the item is picked, it's value will be `picked`, otherwise it'll be `not_picked`
* `qc_status` - If the item has passed all QC checks, it's value will be `passed`. If it has failed a check, it's value will be `fail`.
In some cases, where we do Secondary QC at hub and the item got failed due to Secondary QC, then it's value will be `fail_hub`
* `qc_remarks` - If the item has failed QC checks, then the reasons for failure are shared in this field

eg: In case of QC failed status:

`"picked": "not_picked"`

`"qc_status": "fail"`

`"qc_remarks": "• Brand : No\n• Is product colour as per description ? : No\n• Category : No"`

##Testing your Integration
In order to test your integration, you can start by placing sample order requests on our staging server.
We've created an Order Status Update API as well which works only in the staging environment and it'll allow you to update the order status.
You can use this API to see if the Pull Tracking APIs are working fine or not.


# Group Serviceability

## Unified Pincode Serviceability [/v1/clients/serviceability/?service={service}&page={page}&count={count}&pincodes={pincodes}]
### List All Serviceable Pin Codes  [GET]

By using this endpoint, you can get a list of all Shadowfax serviceable pincodes, as well as the services provided by each of them.

If pagination is not sent as a parameter then by default 25 pin codes will be retrieved.

While triggering the API enter the service for which the list of pincode needs to be fetched.
* The service parameter can be:
    * `seller_pickup` - List all the pincodes where seller pickup is available.
    * `customer_delivery` - List all the pincodes where customer delivery is available.
    * `customer_pickup` - List all the pincodes where customer pickup is available.
    * `seller_delivery` - List all the pincodes where seller delivery is available.
    * `warehouse_pickup` - List all the pincodes where warehouse pickup is available.
    * `warehouse_return` - List all the pincodes where warehouse return or rto is available.


##Requests
This is the URL to make an actual request:<br>
|||
|------------|-----------|
|Staging|`https://dale.staging.shadowfax.in/api/v1/clients/serviceability/?service=customer_pickup&page=1&count=10&pincodes=560016,560017`|
|Production|`https://dale.shadowfax.in/api/v1/clients/serviceability/?service=customer_pickup&page=1&count=10&pincodes=560016,560017`|


+ Parameters
    
    + service:customer_pickup (required, string) - Enter the service for which the list of pincodes needs to be fetched.
    + page:1 (number)- Enter the page number.
    + count:10 (number) - Enter the per page count.
    + pincodes:560017 (number) - Enter the pincodes.

    
