# group Order Cancellation  
## Order Cancellation [/v2/clients/requests/mark_cancel]

### Cancel a Pickup Request [POST]

This endpoint is used to cancel a pickup request. It takes AWB Number or unique client order id of the order along with the cancellation reason as parameters.

* A pickup order can be cancelled before if its status is **NOT** in `Out for Pickup`, `Cancelled` and `Picked` 

If you trigger the cancellation API during `Out for Pickup`(ofp) status, API response would return the `responseMsg` & `responseCode` as `Pickup request cannot be cancelled now` & `400` respectively.

If you trigger the cancellation API during `Picked` status, API response would return the `responseMsg` & `responseCode` as `Pickup request cannot be cancelled now` & `400` respectively.

If you trigger the cancellation API during `Cancelled` status, API response would return the `responseMsg` & `responseCode` as `Pickup request cannot be cancelled now` & `400` respectively.

* Following are the valid Cancellation Remarks. These are entered in the `cancel_remarks` field.
    * Cancelled By Customer
    * Incorrect/ Incomplete contact info
    * Payment Issue

+ Request

    + Body 
    
            { 
                "request_id": "SFXE220250035SK",
                "cancel_remarks ": "Request cancelled by customer"
            }
            
    + Headers
    
            Authorization: Token <token_id here>
            
    + Attributes
    
        + Required Parameters(required, object)
            + request_id(required, string) - AWB number of the order or the client order id of the order. There should be a unique client order id for each order.
            + cancel_remarks(required , string) - Valid options are discussed in the description
            
+ Response 200 (application/json)
    
        {
            "responseMsg": "Request has been marked as cancelled",
            "responseCode": 200
        }

+ Response 401 (application/json)
    
        {
            "status": "FAILED",
            "errorCode": "Authentication credentials not provided",
            "message": "Authentication credentials not provided"
        }


+ Response 200 (application/json)
        {
            "responseMsg": "Invalid Token.",
            "responseCode": 400
        }
        
+ Response 400 (application/json)
    
        {
           "message" : "Invalid AWB Number"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "responseMsg": "Multiple Orders found for the given Request Id",
            "responseCode": 400
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    
        {
            "responseMsg": "Cannot cancel qc order from Out For Pickup",
            "responseCode": 400
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "responseMsg": "Cannot cancel order from Picked",
            "responseCode": 400
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "responseMsg": "Cannot cancel order from Received",
            "responseCode": 400
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "responseMsg": "Pickup request cannot be cancelled now",
            "responseCode": 400
        }
+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "responseMsg": "request_id and cancel_remarks are required",
            "responseCode": 400
        }
        
+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
           "responseMsg": "Order not mapped with the client.",
           "responseCode": 400
        }


#group Escalation API
## Escalation API [/v1/clients/support/issue/]
### Escalation API [POST]
This endpoint to take escalations from clients on real time. Based on the issue category, a ticket would be raised in the system. This API is to take the escalation input from the clients. The action being taken on those tickets .

####Issue Category options 

|Issue Category                        |Issue Category Code  |Validations                                                                                                     |  Order Type           |
|--------------------------------------|---------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------|
| `Delayed Delivery`                   | 1                   |To be passed post an order is successfully picked in system and not delivered post to Estimated Delivery Date   |    Forward          |
| `Expedite Pickup - Customer`         | 2                   |To be passed only if the order is not yet picked from the Customer                                              |    Reverse          |
| `Expedite Pickup - Seller`           | 3                   |To be passed only until the seller pickup is not completed                                                      |    Forward          |
| `Status Mismatch`                    | 4                   |To be passed when there is a mismatch in expected and received order status                                     |    Forward/Reverse  |
| `Delivery Dispute`                   | 5                   |To be passed only post the order is marked Delivered in the system                                              |    Forward          |


+ Request
    + Body
            {
                "awb_number" : "SF00000000TC",
                "issue_category" : 1
            }
    + Headers
            Authorization: Token Authorization
    + Attributes
        + Required Parameters(required, object)
            + awb_number(required, string) - It should be a valid Awb number.
            + issue_category(required , number) - Issue category will be one among choices given in Issue Category options .

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
               "message": "Issue received",
               "status": "SUCCESS"
        }
         

