                    "comment": "Item Received at dc at TestDC2"
                },
                {
                    "created_at": "2022-02-28T10:42:47Z",
                    "current_location": "TestDC2",
                    "state": "Returned To Client",
                    "comment": "Item Return To Origin Delivered at TestDC2"
                }
            ],
            "status": "Returned To Client",
            "scheduled_date": 1645986600000.0,
            "date_created": 1646024179000.0,
            "pickup_type": "regular",
            "slot_start_time": null,
            "slot_end_time": null
        }
    ]
}

+ Response 401 (application/json)
        {
            "status": "FAILED",
            "errorCode": "Authentication credentials not provided",
            "message": "Authentication credentials not provided"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    
        {
           "message" : "Invalid AWB Number"
        }
        
+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "message": "Number of AWBs exceeded. Max count allowed is 50"
        }
        

#group Get POD Details

## Get POD Details [/v1/clients/pod_details/]

### Get POD Details[GET]

Using this API, you can get POD (proof of delivery) details for multiple reverse delivery requests, each defined by their AWB number.
This API will allow you to get pod details for up to 100 AWB numbers.
`To obtain POD details, the order status of the AWB_number's passed must be rto_d`

+ Request (application/json)
    
    + Headers
    
            Authorization: Token 1234567890abc1234567890xyz
            

    + Body

        {
            "awb_numbers": [
                "R18432490TER",
                "R18443342TER"
            ]
        }

+ Response 200 (application/json)


        {
            "message": "Success",
            "pod_details": {
                "R18432490TER": {
                    "recipient": null,
                    "recipient_contact": "None",
                    "recipient_signature": "[[u'https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/sfxdocs/seller/delivery_report/report_1827_1641812277.pdf']]",
                    "recipient_name": "None"
                },
                "R18443342TER": {
                    "recipient": null,
                    "recipient_contact": "None",
                    "recipient_signature": "[u'https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/sfxdocs-mumbai/delivery/pod-images/staging/seller_pod-image-50702-KBWN-1-file.jpeg']",
                    "recipient_name": "None"
                }
            }
        }
    
+ Response 400 (application/json)   

            {
                "message": "AWB does not belong to this client"
            }
            
+ Response 400 (application/json)

            {
                "message": "Incorrect AWB"
            }
            
+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "message": "Max limit on count is 100. Please send a list within 100 AWBs"
        }
          
+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "message": "Incorrect Status"
        }
        
+ Response 401 (application/json)

        {
            "detail": "Invalid token."
        }



# group Order Data Update

## Update QC Flag [/v2/clients/requests/update_qc/]

### Update QC flag for an AWB or SKU [PUT]

This endpoint is used to update the QC flag for a pickup request (or individual SKU) after request creation. Users can update the qc flag either for all the SKUs or for an individual SKU.
QC flag shall not be updated once the AWB is Out of Pickup. If it returns to the hub for pickup on another day, you can then update the QC flag. 

+ Request

    + Body 
    
            { 
                "awb_number": "R12688537SC",
                "qc_flag": true,
                "sku_id": "apple01"
            }
            
    + Headers
    
            Authorization: Token <token_id here>
            
    + Attributes
    
        + Required Parameters(required, object)
            + awb (required, string) - AWB number of the order
            + qc_flag (required, string) - Boolean representing what should be the new QC required flag of the SKU
        + Optional Parameters (optional, object)
            + sku_id (optional, string) - Representing the SKU ID. If this is empty then all SKUs of the AWB Number is updated with the QC flag
            
+ Response 200 (application/json)

        {
            "responseMsg": "QC flags are updated",
            "responseCode": 200
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    
        {
            "responseMsg": "No valid SKU IDs exist for the given AWB Number",
            "responseCode": 400
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "responseMsg": "QC flag can't be changed now since the order is Out For Pickup",
            "responseCode": 400
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
 
        {
            "responseMsg": "Please specify the AWB number",
            "responseCode": 400
        }

+ Response 401 (application/json)

        {
            "status": "FAILED",
            "errorCode": "Authentication credentials not provided",
            "message": "Authentication credentials not provided"
        }

## Update Order Data latest  [/v1/clients/order_update/]

### Request to Update Order Data [POST]
The endpoint allows you to edit customer details, cod amount and payment mode for an order.

The API functionalities are as follows:

* This API cannot be used to update the order status but since the status field is `required` it should be passed as `null`.            
* The API can be used to update customer details along with the Pincode, but the Pincode can only be updated twice per order and only for intra-city orders.
* The mandatory/required attributes should be passed as `null` if they do not need to be updated.
* The Pincode cannot be updated when the current status of the order is `picked`.
* If you try to update the customer details prior to the pickup then the update would occur on pickup details i.e. the end user in case of reverse shipments. If you try to update customer details after pickup, the update would occur on drop details i.e. the seller in case of reverse shipment.

<br><br>The `Authorization` header that should be used while sending request will look like:
<br>
`Token <auth token here>` 
<br>The `Authorization` value itself contains the Word “Token”.

##Requests
This is the URL to make an actual request:<br>
|||
|------------|-----------|
|Staging|`https://dale.staging.shadowfax.in/api/v1/clients/order_update/ `|
|Production|`https://dale.shadowfax.in/api/v1/clients/order_update/ `|

+ Request

    + Attributes
    
        + awb_numbers (required) - Awb number of an order needs to be passed.
        + customer_details  - Pass the customer/ delivery details
            + contact  - Pass customer contact.
            + alternate_contact  - Pass customer contact.
            + customer_address  - Pass customer address.
            + pincode  - Pass customer/delivery pincode.
            + latitude - Pickup customers latitude.
            + longitude - Pickup customers longitude.
       
        + status_update 
            + status  - Pass `null`.
        

    + Body 
    
            {
                "awb_number": "SF36901801TED",
                "customer_details": {
                    "contact": "+919999955555",
                    "alternate_contact": "9999955555",
                    "customer_address": "#253, 2nd cross hebbal",
                    "pincode": 560008,
                    "latitude": "12.00000",
                    "longitude": "77.00000"
                },
              
                "status_update": {
                    "status": null
                }
            }
            
    + Headers
    
            Authorization: Token <token_id here>
            Content-Type: application/json

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    
        {
            "message": "Request accepted."
        }

+ Response 401 (application/json)
    
        {
            "status": "FAILED",
            "errorCode": "Authentication credentials not provided",
            "message": "Authentication credentials not provided"
        }

+ Response 401 (application/json)
    
        {
           "detail": "Invalid token."
        }
        
+ Response 400 (application/json)
    
        {
            "message": "Status transition from recd_at_fwd_hub to ndr is not allowed"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    
        {
            "message": "{\"message\":\"SF36981974TED pincode has been updated 2 times. The Pincode request is stored, will be validated and updated.\"}"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    
        {
            "message": "{\"message\":\"Intercity pincode updates are not allowed\"}"
        }

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    
        {
            "message": "Customer details could not be updated for SF36981985TED due to invalid status. Current status is Delivered to customer"
        }
        
+ Response 400 (application/json)

        {
            "message": "Customer contact number can not be blank"
        }




